# Granot Call Leads Workflow

- `src/parsers/granot/call-leads.ts` parses the Booked Jobs and Follow Up Estimates tables into sectioned preview rows keyed by table header text. The parser is read-only and only reports what is visible in the current Granot page or accessible frames. Each row exposes the Granot `user`/`rep` column as `values.user` / `values.rep` (see `getSalesRepValue()` in `call-leads.ts` and `payloads.ts`).
- `payloads.ts` maps preview rows into the server payloads used for enrichment and booked reconciliation. The `phone` field is included for matching only and must not be treated as a value to write back into `CallLead.phone_number`. The Granot sales-rep column is sent as `granot_crm_username` on both enrichment and booked-reconciliation row payloads. Each row also forwards Granot `from`, `from_zip`, `to`, and `to_zip` so the server can enrich location fields.
- **Location enrichment (call leads, server-side, full diff).** Call leads arrive from RingCentral unenriched — unlike form leads they have no `"not_found"` state sentinel and location fields are usually blank. The extension does not compute location diffs locally; it sends the raw Granot columns to `POST /api/v1/call-leads/enrichment/preview` and `.../sync` (Follow Up Estimates) and the booked-reconciliation endpoints (Booked Jobs). On the server, `callLeadEnrichmentRows.ts` / `bookedCallLeadRows.ts` parse city/state from `from`/`to`, normalize ZIPs, resolve states from ZIP via `getStateCodeForZip()`, and `callLeadEnrichment.service.ts` / `bookedCallLeadReconciliation.service.ts` write every parsed field that differs from the current `CallLead` via `assignIfChanged()`. Whatever Granot provides and the parser can derive is eligible to update; existing non-empty values are overwritten when Granot differs.
- Owner-facing popup summaries and cycle history suppress individual location-field change names while preserving generic updated/will-update status. This affects messaging only; the raw location payloads and server writes remain unchanged.
- `payloads.ts` also defines the sync gates: enrichment rows and booked reconciliation rows are only syncable when the server preview result is `updateable`, `unchanged`, or `updated`.
- `preview.ts` converts a parsed preview response into enrichment and booked-reconciliation payloads, calls the server preview endpoints, and merges results back by `row_id`. If preview fails for one side, the other side can still render.
- `sync.ts` merges returned results back into the preview rows and tallies `updated`, `unchanged`, and `failed` counts. Booked reconciliation treats `conflict`, `booking_missing`, `no_match`, `invalid`, and `failed` as failures.
- **Receiver-agent attribution** runs on the server during enrichment and booked-reconciliation sync (`vantage-main-server/api/services/agents/receiverAgentCrmUsername.ts`). For each syncable row the server normalizes `granot_crm_username`, looks up an Agent by `granot_crm_username`, and sets `receiver_agent` plus provenance (`receiver_agent_source: "extension_crm_username_match"`, `receiver_agent_source_value`, `receiver_agent_name_snapshot`, `receiver_agent_set_at`) only when the Call Lead has no existing `receiver_agent`. Already-linked leads are left unchanged; unmatched usernames surface as warnings on the sync result. A receiver-only match can trigger a write even when no enrichment/reconciliation fields changed.
- `src/entrypoints/popup/ui/salesRep.ts` renders the owner-only **Sales Rep** control on Follow Up Estimates and Booked Jobs call-lead rows once preview resolves a `call_lead_id`. CRM-username match is preferred over first-name match; manual owner links are the only path that can replace an existing `receiver_agent`.
- Preview/sync results may include `receiver_agent_name_snapshot` and `receiver_agent_granot_crm_username` so the popup and auto-sync cycle history reflect linked agents without an extra fetch.
- `cycles.ts` turns enrichment previews into `CycleDetail` entries for auto-sync history, with `updated -> ok`, `unchanged -> unchanged`, `failed/conflict -> failed`, and missing results -> `skipped`.
- The workflow tests live in `src/test/parsers.test.ts` and `src/test/call-leads-payloads.test.ts` (parser shape, payload mapping, sync gates). Server-side location parsing and `assignIfChanged` enrichment are covered in `vantage-main-server/api/services/enrichment/callLeadEnrichmentRows.test.ts` and the booked-reconciliation row parsers.

